{"name":"Wintergreen Shadow","hex":"#4f9e81","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wintergreen","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any evergreen plant.","One of various not closely related evergreen plants, including:\nPlants in shrub genus Gaultheria, commonly known as wintergreen, especially:\nGaultheria procumbens, native to North America, having solitary white flowers and aromatic leaves (checkerberry or teaberry)\nGaultheria humifusa – alpine wintergreen\nGaultheria ovatifolia – western teaberry or Oregon spicy wintergreen\nChimaphila maculata – striped wintergreen, pipsissewa\nPlants in any of several other genera in the herbaceous family Ericaceae, including:\nGenus Pyrola, native to northern temperate and Arctic regions.\nGenus Orthilia\nGenus Moneses\nGenus Chimaphila (prince's pine, pipsissewa)\nSome species of the herbaceous genus Trientalis, in family Primulaceae (chickweed wintergreen)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wintergreen"},{"term":"shadow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dark image projected onto a surface where light (or other radiation) is blocked by the shade of an object.","Relative darkness, especially as caused by the interruption of light; gloom; obscurity."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Unofficial, informal, unauthorized, but acting as though it were.","Having power or influence, but not widely known or recognized."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shadow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wintergreen","blocks":[{"text":"Wintergreen is a group of aromatic plants. The term wintergreen once commonly referred to plants that remain green throughout the winter. The term evergreen is now more commonly used for this characteristic."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/FountainSpringsWintergreen.png/330px-FountainSpringsWintergreen.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wintergreen","wikidata":"Q1785217"},{"title":"Shadow","blocks":[{"text":"A shadow is a dark area on a surface where light from a light source is blocked by an object. In contrast, shade occupies the three-dimensional volume behind an object with light in front of it. The cross-section of a shadow is a two-dimensional silhouette, or a reverse projection of the object blocking the light."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/The_shadow_of_a_musician_playing_transverse_flute.jpg/330px-The_shadow_of_a_musician_playing_transverse_flute.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shadow","wikidata":"Q160020"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Wintergreenleavesandberries.jpg/500px-Wintergreenleavesandberries.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Wintergreenleavesandberries.jpg/1280px-Wintergreenleavesandberries.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Wintergreenleavesandberries.jpg/500px-Wintergreenleavesandberries.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wintergreen from Greeley, Pennsylvania; early December","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWintergreenleavesandberries.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/WintergreenEssentialOil.png/500px-WintergreenEssentialOil.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/WintergreenEssentialOil.png/500px-WintergreenEssentialOil.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wintergreen (Gaultheria procumbens) essential oil","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWintergreenE